course: religion-ethics
lesson: 19
title: Easter and Pentecost
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: On the third day after the crucifixion some women went to Jesus' tomb and found the stone rolled away and the tomb empty. Christians believe Jesus rose from the dead, and they celebrate it at Easter.
explain: The risen Jesus met his friends: Mary Magdalene in the garden, two sad disciples on the road to Emmaus, doubting Thomas, and Peter by the lake, who was forgiven and given a fresh start.
explain: Forty days after Easter Jesus was taken up into heaven, which Christians call the Ascension, and he sent his followers to all nations; fifty days after Easter the Holy Spirit came at Pentecost.
explain: The first Christians shared what they had, ate together, prayed and cared for the poor, and the small group grew into a worldwide church.
explain: For a child today Easter means hope: death and failure are not the end, honest doubts are met with patience, and anyone who has let a friend down can start again.
fact: On the third day women went to Jesus' tomb and found the stone rolled away and the tomb empty.
fact: Christians believe Jesus rose bodily from death and is alive; this is the centre of Christian hope.
fact: Christians call Easter the most important Christian festival.
fact: In John's Gospel Mary Magdalene was the first to meet the risen Jesus; she thought he was the gardener until he said her name.
fact: Two disciples on the road to Emmaus walked with a stranger and recognised Jesus when he broke the bread.
fact: Thomas would not believe until he saw Jesus' wounds; Jesus said, «Blessed are those who have not seen and yet believe».
fact: By the lake the risen Jesus asked Peter three times, «Do you love me?», and told him, «Feed my sheep».
fact: Forty days after Easter Jesus was taken up into heaven; this is called the Ascension.
fact: In the Great Commission Jesus told his followers to go to all nations, make disciples and baptise them.
fact: Fifty days after Easter the Holy Spirit came on the disciples like wind and tongues of fire, and they spoke in many languages; this is Pentecost.
fact: Christians call Pentecost the birthday of the Church.
fact: The first Pentecost happened during a Jewish harvest feast, Shavuot, held fifty days after Passover.
fact: The first Christians shared their belongings, ate together, prayed and cared for the poor (Acts 2).
fact: Other people, such as many atheists and sceptics, do not believe the resurrection happened; Christians and non-Christians can discuss this with respect.
exercise: What did the women find when they went to the tomb? | The stone rolled away and the tomb empty | Soldiers still guarding a sealed tomb with a great stone | Jesus asleep inside the tomb | The tomb filled with flowers
exercise: On which day after the crucifixion was the tomb found empty? | The third day | The first day | The seventh day | The fortieth day
exercise: What do Christians believe happened to Jesus at Easter? | He rose from the dead and is alive | His body was taken away by friends | He only seemed to have died | He became a ghost
exercise: Why do Christians say Easter is their most important festival? | The resurrection is the centre of Christian hope | It has the most chocolate eggs | It has the longest school holiday of the whole year | It is the oldest Jewish festival
exercise: Who did Mary Magdalene think the risen Jesus was at first? | The gardener | A Roman soldier | A Temple priest | An angel from heaven
exercise: When did Mary Magdalene recognise Jesus? | When he said her name | When he showed her his hands | When he broke the bread | When he rode past on a donkey
exercise: When did the two disciples on the road to Emmaus recognise Jesus? | When he broke the bread | When he said their names | When he walked on water | When he climbed a tree
exercise: What did Thomas want before he would believe? | To see Jesus' wounds | To hear the angels sing | To read it in a letter | To see the empty tomb in daylight
exercise: Whom did Jesus call blessed when he spoke to Thomas? | Those who have not seen and yet believe | Those who saw him first | Those who never had a single doubt about him at all | Those who touched his wounds
exercise: How many times did the risen Jesus ask Peter «Do you love me?» | Three times | Once | Twice | Seven times
exercise: What job did Jesus give Peter by the lake? | «Feed my sheep» | «Build a temple» | «Catch more fish» | «Write a Gospel»
exercise: What is the Ascension? | Jesus being taken up into heaven forty days after Easter | The coming of the Holy Spirit at Pentecost | Jesus riding into Jerusalem | The stone rolled from the tomb
exercise: What did Jesus tell his followers in the Great Commission? | Go to all nations, make disciples and baptise them | Stay in Jerusalem and keep the good news a secret from everyone | Build a great church in Rome | Go back to fishing in Galilee
exercise: What came on the disciples at Pentecost? | The Holy Spirit, like wind and tongues of fire | A great flood of rain, like the one in Noah's time | Bread from heaven, like manna | A bright star, like at Christmas
exercise: How many days after Easter is Pentecost? | Fifty | Forty | Three | Twelve
exercise: Why is Pentecost called the birthday of the Church? | The Spirit came and the Church began to grow | Jesus was born on that day | The first church building in Jerusalem opened its doors | Peter was born on that day
exercise: How did the first Christians live, according to Acts 2? | They shared belongings, ate together, prayed and cared for the poor | They lived alone in the desert and never met | They kept their money and hid from others | They only met once a year at Passover
test: My friend says the disciples found the tomb empty, so Pentecost is Easter. What is right? | Easter is the empty tomb; Pentecost is fifty days later, when the Spirit came | Pentecost is the day Jesus was born | Pentecost is the day before Easter | Easter and Pentecost are two names for one day
test: «Ascension and Pentecost same thing innit?» What do you put right? | No: Jesus went up to heaven at the Ascension; the Spirit came at Pentecost | Yes, both are when the Spirit came | No: the Ascension is when Jesus was born | Yes, both are when Jesus rose from the tomb
test: A classmate who is an atheist says, «Dead people don't come back, so Easter's just a story.» What is the most respectful reply? | Christians believe God raised Jesus; I get that you don't, and we can talk about it | You'll be punished for saying that | Everyone in the world believes it, so you're wrong | It doesn't matter, Easter is only about chocolate
test: «I've got loads of questions about God and I'm scared the vicar will be cross». Which story would help? | Doubting Thomas, whose doubts Jesus met with patience | Peter denying Jesus three times by the fire in the courtyard | Judas betraying Jesus for silver | The traders in the Temple
test: «I let my best mate down big time, he'll never trust me again». Which Easter story gives hope? | Peter forgiven and given a job by the lake | The women who found the tomb empty early in the morning | The Ascension of Jesus into heaven on the hill | The tongues of fire that came down at Pentecost
test: Your little brother says Jesus showed himself first to the twelve disciples. Who does John's Gospel say met him first? | Mary Magdalene in the garden | Pilate in his palace | Thomas in a locked room | Peter and John on the road to Emmaus
test: A Jewish friend says Pentecost sounds like their festival of Shavuot. What is true? | Pentecost happened at the Jewish feast fifty days after Passover | Pentecost was invented hundreds of years later by the Church in Rome | Pentecost has nothing to do with any Jewish feast | Pentecost is the Christian name for Hanukkah
test: Your church youth group is planning a food collection. Which part of the lesson does it follow? | The first Christians caring for the poor | The stone rolled away from the tomb on Easter morning | Thomas touching the wounds | The disciples asleep in the garden
test: «Jesus just stayed on earth after Easter, right?» What do Christians believe? | He was taken up to heaven forty days later and is present through the Spirit | He stayed in Jerusalem and lived to be very old | He went back to Nazareth and became a carpenter | He hid in the tomb for forty years
test: A judge asks, «How did a small group of followers become a worldwide church?» Which answer is best reasoned? | They took the Great Commission to heart, travelled and shared their faith | Because a powerful king forced everybody to join the church on the very first day | Because the Bible says so, and that is the only reason | Because no other religions existed at that time
test: Your cousin says the Emmaus disciples knew Jesus at once on the road. What does the story say? | They did not know him until he broke the bread | They knew him because he wore white | They knew him because Peter told them | They knew him at once because he said each of their names
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the condition of the tomb as discovered by the women on the third day? | The stone had been rolled away and the tomb was empty | The tomb was sealed and guarded by soldiers | The body of Jesus remained within the tomb | The tomb had been broken open and destroyed by an earthquake
exam: Ascertain the interval elapsing between Easter and the descent of the Holy Spirit upon the disciples. | Fifty days | Forty days | Three days | Twelve days
exam: Identify the instruction issued by the risen Jesus to Peter subsequent to the threefold question «Do you love me?». | Feed my sheep | Build my temple | Catch more fish | Go home to Galilee
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning the event designated the Ascension. | Jesus was taken up into heaven forty days after Easter | The Holy Spirit descended upon the disciples | Jesus entered Jerusalem upon a donkey | The disciples spoke in many languages
